      "updated_at": "2019-05-27T08:33:33Z",
      "body": "Try that on desktop and Fennec and you'll see that it's not normal behaviour.\r\n\r\nJust because I forget to close a private browsing tab, doesn't mean that private browsing should hijack my browser experience. \r\n\r\nMaybe Fenix is evolving the private browsing experience, to provide more permanence, however that's not expected behaviour and as such, it's probably worth explaining that. But in doing so, what are the impacts to other aspects, do custom tabs act the same? \r\n\r\nWith such an implementation though, of essentially making private browsing an isolated tab group/container, how is it possible that you all dropped the ball and collections glorified bookmarks when they too could've been a tab group/container?\r\n",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
